      "sourceTextSha256": "9e387d9846fefc61e6a07e8f16f9f5c53b70ccc196b4120a0e0e0c2d3ead7413",
      "text": "Ride up into the mountains to Petrópolis, the “Imperial City”, whose land was bought in 1830 by Emperor Pedro I and where his son, Pedro II, Brazil’s last emperor, built his summer palace to escape the heat of Rio. It was here that Pedro II received news of the 1889 coup that ended the monarchy. Visit the Cathedral of Saint Peter of Alcantara, the Imperial Museum, the Crystal Palace and Santos Dumont’s House; optionally, add a visit to the Bohemia Brewery. After the tour, continue to Tiradentes for the night. Approximate distance: 360 km.",
